### 1. Core Architectural Strategy: Ports & Adapters (Hexagonal Isolation)

When vendor SDK models leak across domain files, your core business logic becomes tightly coupled to external API schemas. A breaking change in FedEx's v3 payload or UPS's REST schema will ripple through all 19 domain files.

To fix this cleanly without enterprise over-engineering, adopt **Ports & Adapters (Hexagonal Architecture)** with an **Anti-Corruption Layer (ACL)**:

```
[ Domain Services / Core Logic ]
               │
               ▼ (depends on)
   [ ShippingCarrier Port ] (Domain Interface)
               ▲
               │ (implements)
 ┌─────────────┼──────────────┐
 │             │              │
[FedEx Adapter] [UPS Adapter] [DHL Adapter]
     │              │             │
     ▼              ▼             ▼
(FedEx SDK)     (UPS SDK)     (DHL SDK)
```

1. **Domain Isolation**: Core domain logic imports **zero** carrier SDK types. It depends only on domain entities (`Shipment`, `RateQuote`, `TrackingInfo`) and port interfaces (`ShippingCarrierPort`).
2. **Anti-Corruption Layer**: Each carrier gets a single dedicated adapter folder containing schema mappers (`toDomainShipment`, `toFedExPayload`). Carrier SDK dependencies stay strictly confined to these adapter files.
3. **Canonical Domain Schemas**: Define your unified domain types using Zod or pure TypeScript types representing *your* business needs, not vendor representations.

---

### 2. Concrete Implementation Blueprint

#### A. Define the Domain Port & Canonical Models (`src/domain/shipping/`)

```typescript
// src/domain/shipping/carrier.port.ts

export type CarrierId = "fedex" | "ups" | "dhl";

export interface Address {
  street: string[];
  city: string;
  state: string;
  postalCode: string;
  countryCode: string;
}

export interface PackageSpec {
  weightKg: number;
  dimensionsCm: { length: number; width: number; height: number };
}

export interface CreateShipmentParams {
  origin: Address;
  destination: Address;
  packages: PackageSpec[];
}

export interface LabelResult {
  trackingNumber: string;
  labelBuffer: Buffer;
  format: "pdf" | "zpl";
  carrier: CarrierId;
}

export interface ShippingCarrierPort {
  readonly carrierId: CarrierId;
  createShipment(params: CreateShipmentParams): Promise<LabelResult>;
  getTrackingStatus(trackingNumber: string): Promise<string>;
}
```

#### B. Build Carrier-Specific Adapters (`src/infrastructure/carriers/`)

```typescript
// src/infrastructure/carriers/fedex/fedex.adapter.ts
import type { CreateShipmentParams, LabelResult, ShippingCarrierPort } from "../../../domain/shipping/carrier.port";
import { FedExClient } from "./fedex-sdk-wrapper"; // External vendor SDK import confined here

export class FedExAdapter implements ShippingCarrierPort {
  readonly carrierId = "fedex" as const;

  constructor(private readonly client: FedExClient) {}

  async createShipment(params: CreateShipmentParams): Promise<LabelResult> {
    const payload = this.toFedExPayload(params);
    const response = await this.client.createShipment(payload);

    return {
      trackingNumber: response.output.transactionShipments[0].masterTrackingNumber,
      labelBuffer: Buffer.from(response.output.transactionShipments[0].pieceResponses[0].packageDocuments[0].encodedLabel, "base64"),
      format: "pdf",
      carrier: this.carrierId,
    };
  }

  async getTrackingStatus(trackingNumber: string): Promise<string> {
    const response = await this.client.track(trackingNumber);
    return response.completeTrackResults[0].trackResults[0].latestStatusDetail.statusByLocale;
  }

  private toFedExPayload(params: CreateShipmentParams) {
    return {
      requestedShipment: {
        shipper: { address: { streetLines: params.origin.street, city: params.origin.city } },
        recipients: [{ address: { streetLines: params.destination.street, city: params.destination.city } }],
        requestedPackageLineItems: params.packages.map((pkg) => ({
          weight: { value: pkg.weightKg, units: "KG" },
        })),
      },
    };
  }
}
```

#### C. Carrier Registry / Factory (`src/infrastructure/carriers/carrier.registry.ts`)

```typescript
// src/infrastructure/carriers/carrier.registry.ts
import type { CarrierId, ShippingCarrierPort } from "../../domain/shipping/carrier.port";

export class CarrierRegistry {
  private readonly carriers = new Map<CarrierId, ShippingCarrierPort>();

  register(carrier: ShippingCarrierPort): void {
    this.carriers.set(carrier.carrierId, carrier);
  }

  get(carrierId: CarrierId): ShippingCarrierPort {
    const carrier = this.carriers.get(carrierId);
    if (!carrier) {
      throw new Error(`Carrier ${carrierId} is not configured.`);
    }
    return carrier;
  }
}
